Deliberately empty.

The catalogue's schema is a byte-faithful `pg_dump` of what Alembic's 118
revisions produced, and it lives in ../schema/0001_baseline.sql — the
directory Laravel itself dumps a SQL schema into. It is applied by
`bin/migrate`, which keeps its own ledger (`php_schema_migrations`), refuses a
database Alembic has stamped unless `--adopt` is passed, and reports a
migration edited after it was applied. `php artisan migrate` has none of those
guards, and `.env` points DB_DATABASE at `book_scraper` — so a migration file
placed here is one `artisan migrate` away from writing to production.

Laravel's own skeleton migrations (users, cache, sessions, jobs) were removed
for that reason.

If PHP ever needs a table of its own, give it a separate database or schema
rather than a migration here.
